# ThaiX Core Guardrails

Apply these rules in every task:

- Keep Clean Architecture + DDD + CQRS boundaries strict.
- Keep endpoints thin; business logic stays in Domain/Application.
- Application must not depend on Infrastructure/Presentation.
- Keep EF Core data access in Infrastructure only.
- Use English for code and logs; localize user-facing text via resources.
- Use `ResourceKeys` constants; do not hardcode UI/API messages.
- Use ASCII in source files; `.resx` is the only Unicode exception.
- Keep package versions in `Directory.Packages.props` only.
- Do not auto-stage or auto-commit unless user explicitly requests it.
- Agent asset changes must follow `.cursor/AGENT_SYNC_POLICY.md`.
- If any asset under `.github/`, `.codex/`, or `.cursor/` changes, apply the equivalent change to all three folders in the same turn.
- Before changing a skill, prompt, instruction, or rule, read the corresponding asset in each runtime folder and preserve runtime-specific conventions.

## Rule Routing

- Domain work -> `domain-layer.mdc`
- CQRS/Application work -> `application-layer.mdc`
- EF/Infrastructure work -> `data-access.mdc`
- API integration work -> `external-api.mdc`
- External API application handlers -> `external-api-application.mdc`
- Auth/security in Presentation -> `security-auth.mdc`
- Identity/token persistence in Infrastructure -> `security-identity-infra.mdc`
- Client UI work -> `blazor-ui.mdc`
- Tests work -> `testing.mdc`
